<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal inflation rose 0.1 pct in Dec.</title>
<headline>Portugal inflation rose 0.1 pct in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese consumer prices rose 0.1 percent in December after 0.2 percent in November to give year-on-year inflation of 3.3 percent after 3.0 percent previously, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>Average annual inflation, the government's yardstick, was 3.1 percent in December after 3.1 percent previously</p>
<p> PORTUGUESE INFLATION	  Dec '96	Nov '96  Dec '95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI rise		  0.1	    0.2	 -0.2</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation		3.3	    3.0	  3.4</p>
<p> Average annual inflation	3.1	    3.1	  4.1</p>
<p> Index (base 100 1991)	 132.2	  132.1	128.0</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 3511-3538254  </p>
<p>The biggest increases in prices were reported in:</p>
<p>Food</p>
<p>Cereals and cereal-based products +1.3 percent</p>
<p>Meat and poultry +1.2 percent</p>
<p>Milk and dairy products +0.8 percent</p>
<p>Energy</p>
<p>Gas +1.2 percent</p>
<p>- - - -</p>
<p>The biggest decreases in prices were reported in:</p>
<p>Potatoes -2.5 percent</p>
<p>Eating out -1.3 percent</p>
<p>Hotels and accommodation -1.0 percent</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
